1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,120
What if I told you that, um, basically every single thing you value your ambition,

2
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:08,960
your deepest love for your family, your desire to be a good person.

3
00:00:08,960 --> 00:00:13,200
Or even just, you know, your appreciation for a beautiful sunset is functionally

4
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:16,080
no different than a beaver's blind instinct to build a dam.

5
00:00:16,080 --> 00:00:19,280
Oh, wow. Yeah, that is, that's heavy right out of the gate.

6
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:22,880
Right. That there is absolutely no cosmic weight to any of it. None.

7
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:25,600
It's a completely terrifying proposition, honestly.

8
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:26,080
Yeah.

9
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:30,080
Because we spend our entire lives convinced that the concrete we're standing on,

10
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:33,280
you know, our morals, our loves, our goals.

11
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:36,480
We think that concrete was poured by the universe itself.

12
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:38,560
We assume there's a master blueprint somewhere.

13
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:39,680
Yeah. We really do.

14
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:42,480
And welcome to the deep dive, by the way.

15
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:47,280
Today for you listening, we are basically taking a sledgehammer to that exact foundation,

16
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:49,040
a very methodical sledgehammer.

17
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:54,240
Exactly. We're exploring a profoundly reflective and honestly deeply unnerving essay by

